B.ZR=new A.ct("What is this?","Calculates the height loss Below the Take-Off Surface (BTS) during a Continued Take-Off (CTO) on one engine (OEI) from an elevated offshore helideck, using the chart from AW139 RFM Supplement 97.",null)
B.a_q=new A.ct("Procedure summary","A vertical climb at 400\u2013500 fpm (using 25% \u0394PI) above the helideck reaches the Take-Off Decision Point (TDP) at 25 ft (7.5 m). A nose-down rotation then begins for the flyaway.\n\nEngine failure before TDP: reject back to the helideck (RTO).\nEngine failure at or after TDP: continue the rotation for CTO OEI \u2014 a drop down BTS may be required.\n\nThe procedure always assures deck-edge clearance (\u2265 15 ft vertical, \u2265 35 ft horizontal) and no exposure to ditching.\n\nThe helicopter nose wheel must be positioned 1.5 \u2013 4.0 m from the helideck edge before commencing the manoeuvre.",null)
B.a_7=new A.ct("1 \u2014 Gross Weight","Enter the aircraft all-up weight in kg (5 800 \u2013 7 000 kg) or lb. Toggle the kg/lb button to convert automatically.",null)
B.a_g=new A.ct("2 \u2014 Pressure Altitude",'Pressure altitude of the helideck in feet (\u22121 000 to +1 000 ft).\nUse "Calculate from MSL & QNH" to convert from a QNH setting if needed.',null)
B.a_k=new A.ct("3 \u2014 OAT","Outside air temperature in \xb0C.",null)
B.a_o=new A.ct("4 \u2014 Headwind","Unfactored headwind component in knots. The maximum is automatically limited to the upper boundary of the wind nomogram for the current conditions and adjusts as inputs change.",null)
B.a_n=new A.ct("Result","Height loss BTS in feet. 0 ft means conditions fall below the chart's lower boundary \u2014 no meaningful drop down is required.\n\nThe red trace shows: PA/OAT (left graph) \u2192 wind nomogram (centre) \u2192 GW curve (right graph) \u2192 height loss on the x-axis.",null)
B.a_3=new A.ct("Helideck height requirement","If a drop down is indicated, the helideck elevation above the sea (or obstacles) must exceed the computed drop down plus the clearance margin required by the Competent Authority. There must be no obstacles beyond and below the deck edge.",null)
B.ZV=new A.ct("Chart","Tap the chart to open it full-screen with pan and zoom.",null)
B.aNA=s([B.ZR,B.a_q,B.a_7,B.a_g,B.a_k,B.a_o,B.a_n,B.a_3,B.ZV],t.p)
B.t4=s(["S","M","T","W","T","F","S"],t.s)
B.ZX=new A.ct("What is this tool?","Calculates the remaining serviceable life of the Number 1 and Number 2 starter generator brush sets, per the detailed inspection procedure (39-A-24-31-01-01A-31AA-A).",null)
B.a_0=new A.ct("Aircraft & generator identification","Optionally record the aircraft registration, each generator's serial number, and free-text comments. These are included in the shared/downloaded PDF but do not affect the calculation.",null)
B.a_d=new A.ct("1 \u2014 Measure the shortest brush","Find the shortest brush in the set and measure its length (Y). A new brush is 17.78 mm (0.7 in) long.\n\nTip: scroll wheel on the field to adjust the value.",null)
B.a__=new A.ct("2 \u2014 Enter operated hours","Enter the brush operated hours (T) from the Aircraft Log Book.",null)
B.a_6=new A.ct("3 \u2014 Visual checks","Tick any box that applies after examining the brush with a strong light: damaged, cracked, or seated area unsatisfactory (below 85% minimum, per detail C/D of the IETP figure). Any of these alone requires discarding the brush set.",null)
B.a_9=new A.ct("4 \u2014 Read the result","Brush wear (X) = 17.78 \u2212 Y.\nWear rate (Z) = X \xf7 T.\nServiceable life (W) = Y \xf7 Z.\n\nThe brush set is flagged for discard if any visual check is ticked, or if the calculated serviceable life is below 150 hours.",null)
B.a_2=new A.ct("5 \u2014 Share PDF","Once at least one generator has valid inputs, download/share buttons appear. They generate a PDF report with both generators' results.",null)
B.a_p=new A.ct("Safety","Always refer to up-to-date official AW139 maintenance publications before performing any maintenance action. This tool is for reference only.",null)
